      "ihh:notes": "Resolves the open rights question on EIN-M-0049 with the National Archives' own item-level statement: the DocsTeach document page (registry entry docsteach, part_of nara; snapshot EIN-S-0106) gives 'Rights: Public Domain, Free of Known Copyright Restrictions.' for this letter (National Archives Identifier 16608874). EIN-M-0049 recorded the catalog file unit's useRestriction 'Unrestricted' and was refuted for that mismatch; a person should reject EIN-M-0049 in favour of this record. The letter is pages 2-3 of the catalog PDF psfa0064.pdf (21 pages: Sachs letter pp. 4-6, FDR memo to General Watson 13 Oct 1939 p. 7, draft secretary reply p. 8, FDR reply p. 9). Stop 4 (Nassau Point, Peconic, 1939).\nAuthorship set on 2026-10-20: private (Albert Einstein, Leo Szilard, Alexander Sachs) (private-writings rule, DECISIONS 2026-10-20): signed by Einstein; DocsTeach names Szilard and Sachs as collaborators.\nEdit lock (2026-10-20): rights fields changed after verification; adversary verdict 'supported' by codex:gpt-6.1-sol (run adv-einstein-docs-2026-10-20b, 2026-10-20) cleared for re-verification."
