      "ihh:notes": "Round 9 records (research R9-M-EIN-007, 2026-10-29). Chapter: einstein/history. Shows: The typed White House memorandum with F. D. R.'s initials (page 7 of the Sachs file). Holder date: 1939-10-13. Resolution: PDF page 720 x 702 pt; preview rendered at 120 dpi. Preview previews/ein-history-fdr-memo-1939-10-13-07.jpg sha256 62b47b4b922f8008ba1da5a020a3c3c150f3d3b7efcfee117af08fd90134303a. Supports facts: EIN-F-0110, EIN-F-0135. Rights basis: NARA 'Unrestricted' + federal authorship (3.4.1). Page 7 only; the file also holds Sachs's and Einstein's private letters (Sachs d. 1973 -> his letters link-only). Pages shown: 7 (memorandum for General Watson, 13 Oct 1939) and 9 (the President's reply to Einstein, 19 Oct 1939, carbon), research R9-M-EIN-008 folded into this record. url: the file unit's digital object psfa0064.pdf (catalog.archives.gov/id/16608874 is the url of the rejected EIN-M-0049, the Einstein letter, superseded by EIN-M-0063).\nAuthorship set on 2026-10-30: federal (Franklin D. Roosevelt) (private-writings rule, DECISIONS 2026-10-20): round 9 records 2026-10-30."
